<section aria-label="RPG Maker MV save editing guide" class="not-prose mt-14 space-y-12">
  <!-- Intro Summary Card -->
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-800 p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">What is an .rpgsave editor?</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
        An <strong>.rpgsave editor</strong> reads an RPG Maker MV save slot and lets you change compatible values
        before rebuilding the file. SaveFileTool runs this workflow in your browser: choose your desktop save above,
        check the detected gold value, make a small change, and download a zip containing both the edited save and
        an unchanged original backup. No account or installer is required.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
        An MV save records more than money—party members, inventory, map position, switches, variables, and quest
        progress. A number that looks editable may control an event rather than a resource. <strong>Gold is the
        verified edit path here</strong>; other detected fields remain candidates until you verify them in your game.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Save Folder Location with Visual Diagram -->
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-slate-50/70 dark:bg-gray-800/50 p-6 sm:p-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Where to find RPG Maker MV save files</h2>
    <figure class="my-6 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 shadow-sm">
      <img
        src="/images/guides/save-folder-location.jpg" width="1376" height="768"
        alt="Desktop folder tree comparing RPG Maker MV www/save/file1.rpgsave and RPG Maker MZ save/file1.rmmzsave locations"
        class="block h-auto w-full"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption class="border-t border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800/90 px-4 py-2.5 text-center text-xs text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 dark:text-gray-300">
        Pick a numbered progress slot like <code>file1.rpgsave</code>—skip <code>config.rpgsave</code> and <code>global.rpgsave</code>.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 p-5">
        <div class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">Desktop Windows</div>
        <h3 class="mt-1 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Check <code>www/save/</code> or <code>save/</code></h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          Start in the folder containing the game executable. Many packaged MV games keep saves in <code>www/save/</code>;
          others and editor test projects use <code>save/</code> directly. Plugins can change this location.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 p-5">
        <div class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-emerald-600">Choose the Right Slot</div>
        <h3 class="mt-1 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Use numbered slots only</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          Save once in game and match the latest timestamp (e.g. <code>file1.rpgsave</code>). Files named
          <code>global.rpgsave</code> or <code>config.rpgsave</code> store settings and save lists, not party gold.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 p-5">
        <div class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-amber-600">Browser-Hosted Games</div>
        <h3 class="mt-1 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Stored in browser storage</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          “Play in browser” MV games save to browser storage instead of disk. Use the game's own export feature if
          available; renaming a saved webpage to <code>.rpgsave</code> will not create a valid save.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Step-by-Step Workflow with Visual Diagram -->
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-800 p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Change gold and load the edited save</h2>
    <figure class="my-6 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-gray-800 shadow-sm">
      <img
        src="/images/guides/safe-edit-workflow.jpg" width="1376" height="768"
        alt="Four-step safe RPG Maker MV save editing workflow: backup original, edit gold locally, extract ZIP, and verify in game"
        class="block h-auto w-full"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption class="border-t border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800/90 px-4 py-2.5 text-center text-xs text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 dark:text-gray-300">
        Safe backup-first workflow: every export bundles the rebuilt slot alongside your untouched original file.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <ol class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <li class="rounded-xl border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900/60 p-4">
        <span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-600 text-xs font-bold text-white">1</span>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Record starting gold</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Note your current gold, save to a known slot, and close the game so it cannot overwrite your changes.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-xl border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900/60 p-4">
        <span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-600 text-xs font-bold text-white">2</span>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Keep a separate backup</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Copy the numbered <code>.rpgsave</code> file to another folder with its original filename intact.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-xl border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900/60 p-4">
        <span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-600 text-xs font-bold text-white">3</span>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Verify detected value</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Open the file above and confirm the displayed gold matches your game menu before editing.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-xl border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900/60 p-4">
        <span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-600 text-xs font-bold text-white">4</span>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Edit one value first</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Enter a modest gold amount and leave other fields untouched on your first test to keep troubleshooting simple.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-xl border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900/60 p-4">
        <span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-600 text-xs font-bold text-white">5</span>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Extract the ZIP package</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Place the rebuilt numbered file into the game's save directory—not the <code>.zip</code> archive or backup-prefixed copy.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-xl border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900/60 p-4">
        <span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-600 text-xs font-bold text-white">6</span>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Load &amp; confirm in game</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Reopen the game, choose Continue, and inspect gold, party, and map position before deleting your backup.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <!-- Verification Evidence Highlight -->
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-emerald-200 dark:border-emerald-800/70 bg-emerald-50/70 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 p-6 sm:p-8">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
      <span class="rounded-full bg-emerald-600 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-white">Verified Workflow</span>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-emerald-950 dark:text-emerald-200">What the MV gold verification covers</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-100">
        Our verification used the official <strong>RPG Maker MV 1.6.1</strong> trial package on Windows. The game
        created an original <code>.rpgsave</code> with <strong>1234 gold</strong>; the local editor changed it to
        <strong>98765</strong>, exported it, and the game loaded the rebuilt save cleanly with the new gold displayed.
        Control values remained intact (variable 1 = 42, switch 1 = true, item 1 qty = 3), and the original backup
        matched byte for byte.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-100">
        This evidence comes from an official trial project rather than third-party commercial games. It confirms the
        standard MV gold workflow, while games with custom save plugins, integrity checks, or modified data layouts
        still require a small test edit and in-game load check.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- MV vs MZ Comparison Table -->
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-800 p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">MV .rpgsave and MZ .rmmzsave are different formats</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
      Choose the editor by your file's original extension rather than the game's art style. Renaming an extension does
      not convert its compression or engine objects. Older formats (<code>.rxdata</code>, <code>.rvdata</code>,
      <code>.rvdata2</code>) belong to earlier RPG Maker generations and are outside this page's published support.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-5 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full border-collapse text-left text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900/60 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 dark:text-gray-300">
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Engine</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Extension</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Standard Compression</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Typical Save Path</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Editor</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100 dark:divide-gray-700">
          <tr class="bg-blue-50/40 dark:bg-blue-950/30">
            <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">RPG Maker MV</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3"><code>.rpgsave</code></td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">LZString + Base64</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3"><code>www/save/</code> or <code>save/</code></td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300">Current page</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">RPG Maker MZ</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3"><code>.rmmzsave</code></td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">pako (zlib/deflate)</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3"><code>save/</code></td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3">
              <a href="/editor/rpg-maker-mz/" class="font-semibold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline">Open MZ Save Editor &rarr;</a>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Plugins & Privacy Two-Column Cards -->
  <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 dark:border-amber-800/70 bg-amber-50/60 dark:bg-amber-950/40 p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-950 dark:text-amber-200">Why plugins and custom saves may not work</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-100">
        MV developers can install plugins that add fields, encrypt saves, change compression, or move data into another
        container. Parsing a file does not guarantee that every field has the expected meaning or passes custom checks.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-100">
        If a rebuilt file fails to load, restore your backup and retry a smaller gold-only edit on a fresh slot.
        Repeatedly renaming or recompressing the file will not fix a custom plugin layout.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-gray-800 p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Privacy, backups, and the 10 MB limit</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        Files are read and rebuilt locally in your browser—save contents are never uploaded to a server. Every download
        includes your original backup, and optional local history stays strictly in browser storage on your device.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        Files over <strong>10 MB</strong> are rejected. Select the numbered <code>.rpgsave</code> file itself rather
        than a full project folder or archive, and do not delete sections of a plugin-heavy save to shrink it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Collapsible FAQ Accordion -->
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-800 p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">RPG Maker MV save editing questions</h2>
    <div class="mt-5 space-y-3">
      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50/70 dark:bg-gray-900/50 open:bg-white dark:open:bg-gray-800">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between p-4 font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
          <h3>Why does the game still show my old gold?</h3>
          <span class="ml-4 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">&#9662;</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="px-4 pb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          Check that you extracted the edited file from the zip, replaced the correct numbered slot, and restarted the
          game before loading. Multiple installations, a still-running game, or cloud sync can restore an older copy;
          compare file modification times before retrying.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50/70 dark:bg-gray-900/50 open:bg-white dark:open:bg-gray-800">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between p-4 font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
          <h3>Can I open the .rpgsave file in a text editor instead?</h3>
          <span class="ml-4 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">&#9662;</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="px-4 pb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          A standard MV save stores LZString-compressed data, so its raw text is not directly editable JSON. Editing
          characters manually can corrupt the save. Use a compatible editor to decode and rebuild it while keeping your
          original backup.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50/70 dark:bg-gray-900/50 open:bg-white dark:open:bg-gray-800">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between p-4 font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
          <h3>Can this editor change quest switches or inventory safely?</h3>
          <span class="ml-4 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">&#9662;</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="px-4 pb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          Those fields are candidates whose meaning depends on the specific game and its plugins. Folder Mode can load
          labels from the game's JSON data files to help identify IDs, but labels are not a compatibility guarantee.
          Test one small change in a disposable slot first.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50/70 dark:bg-gray-900/50 open:bg-white dark:open:bg-gray-800">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between p-4 font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
          <h3>What should I do if the edited slot will not load?</h3>
          <span class="ml-4 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">&#9662;</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="px-4 pb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          Close the game and restore the original numbered file from your backup or the downloaded zip. Confirm the
          restored slot loads normally, then retry with a conservative gold-only edit while keeping the failing copy
          separate from your working backup.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
